{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nusing lli = long long;\nconst int MAXN = 7;\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\nconst lli E100 = 570000004;\nint n;\nint g[MAXN][MAXN];\nlli nxt[1<<MAXN][1<<MAXN];\nint bitcnt[1<<MAXN];\nvector<int> S[MAXN+1];\nint id[1<<MAXN];\nint memo[MAXN][1<<MAXN];\nbool vis[MAXN][1<<MAXN];\n\nint dfs(int i, int msk) {\n    if (msk == 0) return 0;\n    if (i == n) return 1;\n    if (vis[i][msk]) return memo[i][msk];\n    lli res = 0;\n    for (int s = 0; s < (1<<n); ++s) {\n        lli prob = 1;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            if (s & (1 << j)) \n                prob = (prob * g[i][j]) % MOD;\n            else \n                prob = (prob * ((1 - g[i][j] + MOD) % MOD)) % MOD;\n        }\n        int next_mask = 0;\n        for (int j = 0; j < 35; ++j) \n            if ((1LL << j) & msk) \n                next_mask |= nxt[s][S[i][j]];\n        res = (res + prob * dfs(i+1, next_mask)) % MOD;\n    }\n    vis[i][msk] = true;\n    return memo[i][msk] = (int)(res % MOD);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    scanf(\"%d\", &n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) \n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) { \n            int val;\n            scanf(\"%d\", &val);\n            g[i][j] = (int)((lli)val * E100 % MOD);\n        }\n    for (int i = 1; i < (1<<n); ++i) \n        bitcnt[i] = bitcnt[i ^ (i & -i)] + 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < (1<<n); ++i) {\n        id[i] = S[bitcnt[i]].size();\n        S[bitcnt[i]].push_back(i);\n    }\n    for (int i = 1; i < (1<<n); ++i) \n        for (int j = 0; j < (1<<n); ++j) \n            for (int k = 0; k < n; ++k) \n                if ((i & (1<<k)) && !(j & (1<<k)))\n                    nxt[i][j] |= 1LL << id[j|1<<k];\n    int result = dfs(0, 1);\n    result = (result % MOD + MOD) % MOD;\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", result);\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nsys.setrecursionlimit(10000)\n\nMOD = 1000000007\nMAXN = 7\nE100 = 570000004\n\ndef main():\n    n = int(input())\n    g = [[0] * MAXN for _ in range(MAXN)]\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        row = list(map(int, input().split()))\n        for j in range(n):\n            val = row[j]\n            g[i][j] = int((val * E100) % MOD)\n    \n    # Precompute bit counts\n    bitcnt = [0] * (1 << MAXN)\n    for i in range(1, 1 << MAXN):\n        bitcnt[i] = bitcnt[i & (i - 1)] + 1\n    \n    # Build S and id arrays\n    S = [[] for _ in range(MAXN + 1)]\n    id_map = [0] * (1 << MAXN)\n    \n    for i in range(1 << n):\n        cnt = bitcnt[i]\n        id_map[i] = len(S[cnt])\n        S[cnt].append(i)\n    \n    # Precompute nxt array\n    nxt = [[0] * (1 << MAXN) for _ in range(1 << MAXN)]\n    for i in range(1, 1 << n):\n        for j in range(1 << n):\n            for k in range(n):\n                if (i & (1 << k)) and not (j & (1 << k)):\n                    nxt[i][j] |= 1 << id_map[j | (1 << k)]\n    \n    # Memoization\n    memo = [[-1] * (1 << MAXN) for _ in range(MAXN)]\n    vis = [[False] * (1 << MAXN) for _ in range(MAXN)]\n    \n    def dfs(i, msk):\n        if msk == 0:\n            return 0\n        if i == n:\n            return 1\n        if vis[i][msk]:\n            return memo[i][msk]\n        \n        res = 0\n        for s in range(1 << n):\n            prob = 1\n            for j in range(n):\n                if s & (1 << j):\n                    prob = (prob * g[i][j]) % MOD\n                else:\n                    prob = (prob * ((1 - g[i][j] + MOD) % MOD)) % MOD\n            \n            next_mask = 0\n            for j in range(35):  # 35 is safe upper bound for n <= 7\n                if (1 << j) & msk:\n                    next_mask |= nxt[s][S[i][j]]\n            \n            res = (res + prob * dfs(i + 1, next_mask)) % MOD\n        \n        vis[i][msk] = True\n        memo[i][msk] = res % MOD\n        return memo[i][msk]\n    \n    result = dfs(0, 1)\n    result = (result % MOD + MOD) % MOD\n    print(result)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00018153927521780133, -9.536738616588991e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0028805925976485014, -0.00019643761334009469, -0.07890550047159195, -0.043830085545778275, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.2053474822314456e-05, -3.0278701160568744e-05, -2.8013790142722428e-05, 0.0, -2.1219027985353023e-05, -6.6756979322235566e-06, -9.775113539944869e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -0.08896344900131226, -0.2621910870075226, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -6.615896563744172e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, -3.6954811548639555e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -5.483612312673358e-06, -1.3828182090946939e-05, -0.34849807620048523, -1.680836794548668e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.0003815161471720785, -1.311301275563892e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.38